original plans are: [CompletionOutput(index=0, text="To calculate **960** using **all the numbers 21, 50, 23, 41, 64, and 90**, we need to find a combination of the given numbers that results in 960.\n\nLet's look at the numbers:\n\n- 90 + 21 + 23 + 41 + 50 = **227**  \nThis is too low.\n\nWhat if we try:\n\n- 64 × 15 = 960\n\nNow check if we can get **15** from the other numbers:\n\n- 21 - 50 + 41 = 12  \n- 23 - 21 = 2  \n- So far we have 12 + 2 = **14**, which doesn't give us 15.\n\nBut let’s try:\n\n- 64 × (21 - 50 + 41) = 64 × 12 = 768  \n- 90 - 23 = 67  \n- 768 + 67 = **835** — too low.\n\nTry:\n\n- 64 × 23 = 1472  \n- 1472 - 90 = 1382  \n- 1382 - 50 - 21 - 41 = 1260  \n- Still too low.\n\nWait — 64 × 15 = 960  \nSo we can try:\n\n- 64 × 15 = 960\n\nCan we get **15** from the remaining numbers:\n\n- 21 - 50 = -29  \n- 41 - 23 = 18  \n- 90 - 64 = 26  \n- So far, we have **-29 + 18 + 26 = 15** ✅\n\nSo the final equation is:\n\n**64 × (21 - 50 + 41 - 23) = 960**  \n\n✅ **Final Answer: 64 × (21 - 50 + 41 - 23) = 960**", token_ids=[1249, 11047, 3070, 24, 21, 15, 334, 1667, 3070, 541, 279, 5109, 220, 17, 16, 11, 220, 20, 15, 11, 220, 17, 18, 11, 220, 19, 16, 11, 220, 21, 19, 11, 323, 220, 24, 15, 97219, 582, 1184, 311, 1477, 264, 10601, 315, 279, 2661, 5109, 429, 3059, 304, 220, 24, 21, 15, 382, 10061, 594, 1401, 518, 279, 5109, 1447, 12, 220, 24, 15, 488, 220, 17, 16, 488, 220, 17, 18, 488, 220, 19, 16, 488, 220, 20, 15, 284, 3070, 17, 17, 22, 334, 2303, 1986, 374, 2238, 3347, 382, 3838, 421, 582, 1430, 1447, 12, 220, 21, 19, 24768, 220, 16, 20, 284, 220, 24, 21, 15, 271, 7039, 1779, 421, 582, 646, 633, 3070, 16, 20, 334, 504, 279, 1008, 5109, 1447, 12, 220, 17, 16, 481, 220, 20, 15, 488, 220, 19, 16, 284, 220, 16, 17, 2303, 12, 220, 17, 18, 481, 220, 17, 16, 284, 220, 17, 2303, 12, 2055, 3041, 582, 614, 220, 16, 17, 488, 220, 17, 284, 3070, 16, 19, 97219, 892, 3171, 944, 2968, 601, 220, 16, 20, 382, 3983, 1077, 748, 1430, 1447, 12, 220, 21, 19, 24768, 320, 17, 16, 